  "raw_text": "122\n\nKupia swapni\n \n(\ndb-Impakan Sturka 34:6,Lawana Nani 103:8\n)\n \n–\n \nsoft-hearted, compassionate, reasonable\n \n/ suave,\ncompasivo, razonable\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-04/20\n):\n \nYawan dîa daukaia sip sa wan baska kum ba kupia swapni apia sa kaka?\n \n–\n \nWhat are we able to do if\nour boss is not reasonable?\n \n/ ¿Qué podemos hacer si nuestro jefe no es razonable?)\n\nKupia swapnikira\n \n(\nbh43\n)\n \n–\n \nsoft-heartedly, compassionately, reasonably\n \n/ de corazón suave, compasivo,\nrazonablemente\n\nKupia tahpla\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nbitter heart\n \n/ corazón amargado\n\nKupia tikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto lose hope, to lose heart, to become disheartened, to frighten\n \n/ perder la esperanza,\ndesanimarse, asustar\n\nKupia turbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto disturb the heart, to become disturbed in the heart, to cause anxiety in the heart\n \n/\nperturbar el corazón, causar ansiedad en el corazón\n\nKupia turban\n \n–\n \ndisturbed heart, anxious heart\n \n/ corazón perturbado, corazón ansioso\n\nKupia turbanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ndisturbance in the heart, anxiety in the heart\n \n/ alteración en el corazón, ansiedad\nen el corazón\n\nKupia turbanka\n \nlâka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nanxiety, anxiety of heart\n \n/ ansiedad, ansiedad del corazón\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nwqu\n-\n04/20\n):\n \nKupia turbanka l\nâ\nka ba nahki upla kum kum ra ambuk munisa?\n \n–\n \nHow does anxiety of\n\nheart hurt some people?\n \n/ ¿Cómo afecta la ansiedad del corazón a algunas personas?\n)\n\nKupia tuskaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto provoke, to offend, to induce, to incite, to instigate, to bother\n \n/ provocar, ofender, inducir,\nincitar, instigar, molestar\n\nKupia tuskanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nprovocation, offence\n \n/ provocación, ofensa\n\nKupia wilinkira\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwilling heart\n \n/ corazón dispuesto\n\nKupia wina aisaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto speak from the heart\n \n/ hablar desde el corazón\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth-2,11\n):\n \nKupiam wina aisas\n \n–\n \nSpeak from your heart\n \n/\n \nHabla desde tu corazon)\n\nKupia wina padin munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto forgive from the heart\n \n/ perdonar desde el corazón\n\nKupia wirha\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nheavy heart, anguish of heart, deep sadness\n \n/ pesadez en el corazón, angustia en el corazón,\n\nprofunda tristeza\n\nKupia yamni lâka\n \n(\nbh\n) (n/s)\n \n–\n \nkindness\n \n/ amabilidad\n\nKupias\n \n–\n \nheartless\n \n/ despiadado\n\nKura\n \n(\ndb\n,\ndictu\n,\nbh\n;\n \nKurra\n-dict\n)\n \n(adj,n/s)\n \n–\n \nunripe, immature, young coconut\n \n/ inmaduro, coco joven\n\nKuku kura\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nyoung coconut\n \n/ coco joven\n\n(Note/Nota: Some just say\n \nKura\n \nto describe a young coconut / Algunos solo dicen\n \nKura\n \npara describir un coco joven)\n\nTwi kura\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngreen grass, young green grass, green vegetation\n \n/ pasto verde, hierba verde, hierba verde\n\ntierna\n, vegetaci\nó\nn verde\n\nKurbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto scratch\n \n/ rascar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nfy116\n):\n \nJob sumi kriwan pîska kum ni ai taya ba kurbi kan\n \n–\n \nJob was scratching himself from a broken piece of a jar\n \n/ Job se\nrascaba con un trozo roto de un frasco)\n\nKusbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto carve, to whittle, to scrape\n \n/ tallar, raspar\n\nKusbi sakaia\n \n(\ndb\n)\n \n–\n \nto scrape and remove\n \n/ raspar y quitar\n\nKuskuspiram\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ngrackle, bird similar to a raven\n \n/ sanate (zanate), ave parecida la\n \nCuervo\n\nKus\nwa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nsmall freshwater turtle\n, jicotea (\ndictu)\n \n/ tortuga pequena de\n \nagua dulce\n,\n\njicotea (dictu)\n\nKuswa kati\n \n–\n \nFebruary\n \n/ febrero\n\n(Lit:\n \nturtle moon\n \n/ luna tortuga)\n\nKut munaia\n \n(\ndict,dictu,fy,lv\n)\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto court a\n \nperson, to date a person\n \n/ cortejar a una persona, salir con una persona\n\nKut muni nani\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npeople who are dating\n \n/ personas que estan saliendo\n, personas que estan jalando\n\nKut takaia\n \n(\ndb,fy,lv\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto court, to date\n \n/ cortejar, salir\n\nKut takaia l\nâ\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \ncourtship\n \n/ noviazgo\n\nKutbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto surround, to encircle, to fence in\n \n/ rodear, cercar\n\nKir kutbaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto completely surround, to encircle all around\n \n/ rodear completamente, rodear todo\n\nKutbi kir\n \n–\n \nsurrounding all around\n \n/ rodeando todo\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nWitnis ailal kutbi kir wan bri\n \n–\n \nWe have many witnesses surrounding all around us\n \n/ Tenemos muchos testigos\nrodeándonos a nuestro alrededor)",
